Board verification failed: all template replies became empty strings (even for a single tool), and r95 is a regression.

Cause: MCP tools executed in the pi do not go through the socket. In rust/crates/middleware-service/src/agent/real_tool_executor.rs:50, UdsToolExecutor::execute directly returns ToolOutcome::Ok{result:String::new()} for such calls. As a result, record_start marks the tool_call_id as started (with say as None), and the subsequent ToolCallEnd with say is discarded in record_end because the id already exists. The old code overwrote, and since End arrives last, it worked.

Fix requirements, complete in one pass:
1. Change deduplication to save each call's say by tool_call_id (in first-occurrence order). Write only when Start parses a say; when End has say, write or overwrite the value for the same id; when End has ok=false, remove the say for that id. Each call is counted only once.
2. When rendering, take calls with say in order, keep only one for consecutive identical values, and join with '，'.
3. Add tests that must include the real shape: Start's outcome is Ok{result:""}, End carries say. Test both single-tool and two-tool cases. Keep existing tests.
4. Gate: cd rust && cargo test -p middleware-service --features service must all pass; changed files must have no clippy warnings; only modify handler.rs; commit separately (with the original footer). Don't write a plan, don't stop to ask.
